model {
  extend basalt.catalog {
    metadata {
      constraint "The database adapter retains its legacy provider identity, auth declarations and every existing API tool name. A separate sign-in provider uses the configured hosted client and requires its exact reviewed scopes to be confirmed before saving an account; refusal records requested, reported and missing access with recovery. Automatic registration is a limited fallback only when no hosted client is configured. Host protocol p39 passes grant-scoped oauthScopes metadata from the same credential snapshot without exposing credential fields; retained adapters omit it. Known new grants filter tools; unknown legacy and DCR grants remain explicitly unknown without changing their previous tool behavior. Service-token-only operations retain their old names and gain aliases in the generic tool section, whose action opens the normal token form. Required scope confirmation augments the current first-party client definition and default scopes; it cannot replace other client validation or alter released protocol 39 adapters."
    }
  }
}
